			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "waSYHEWU",
			"originalText": "In distributed systems, many computers (called nodes) work together over a network. Consensus means all these nodes must agree on a single value or decision — even when things go wrong, like network delays or crashed machines.",
